03 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533958 true] [17592186268841 1111 #uuid "525c0a59-b99b-596e-8cc6-57c210550162" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268842 1034 "-\\pi " 13194139533958 true] [17592186268842 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533958 true] [17592186268842 1111 #uuid "d0fdc981-e8e2-50b9-878d-7f3abd8e9c6b" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268843 1034 "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268843 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533958 true] [17592186268843 1111 #uuid "b0658aa8-64b3-56c3-9715-b62e26aad75a" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268844 1017 #edb/ref 17592186268845 13194139533958 true] [17592186268844 1089 "q-43659" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268844 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533958 true] [17592186268844 1100 "What is the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268844 1113 #uuid "e78d2563-d22e-5b86-b89f-f6aab65d4ec5" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268844 1145 "Let's recall some of the basic properties of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x:$\n\n- The domain is all real numbers.\n\n- There is a zero at $x=0.$\n\n- The function is negative over $(-\\infty ,0)$ and positive over $(0,\\infty ).$\n\n- The function is strictly increasing in its entire domain.\n\n- $y\\to -\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (from above) as $x\\to -\\infty .$\n\n- $y\\to \\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (from below) as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\n- The lines $y=\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}$ are horizontal asymptotes of the function.\n\nOf the given functions, the only one that has all of these properties is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13963369/assets/d7984b9098d02bfc2b1e9a422aef919533abce54fbb94117e709c7613b0870a3.png)" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268846 13194139533958 true] [17592186268845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268847 13194139533958 true] [17592186268845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268848 13194139533958 true] [17592186268845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268849 13194139533958 true] [1759218626