5452 13194139533958 true] [17592186268850 1111 #uuid "4e23f243-f662-5d5e-ae4a-f9e307090dc6" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268851 1017 #edb/ref 17592186268852 13194139533958 true] [17592186268851 1089 "q-65979" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268851 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533958 true] [17592186268851 1100 "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$\n\n- $(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$\n- $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{4})$\n- $(-1,\\frac{3\\pi }{4})$" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268851 1113 #uuid "84a20de8-bfb9-5771-87ce-4b0eb965dc43" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268851 1145 "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First,  we consider the point $(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}},\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},0)$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(-1,\\frac{3\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{3\\pi }{4},-1)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ does **not** lie within this range. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(-1,\\frac{3\\pi }{4})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268852 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268853 13194139533958 true] [17592186268852 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268854 13194139533958 true] [17592186268852 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268855 13194139533958 true] [17592186268852 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268856 13194139533958 true] [17592186268852 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268857 13194139533958 true] [17592186268852 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533958 true] [17592186268852 1041 "selection" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268852 1104 #edb/ref 17592186268854 13194139533958 true] [17592186268852 1110 #uuid "d65f976a-9a55-56d0-8d01-c163185aff72" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268853 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268853 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533958 true] [17592186268853 1111 #uuid "d0c4e0c0-0c8c-5ce7-b1ae-37a48c88aa08" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268854 1034 "I only" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268854 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533958 true] [17592186268854 1111 #uuid "f165483b-b658-5a50-adc8-d333f991d806" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268855 1034 "III only" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268855 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533958 true] [17592186268855 1111 #uuid "75a61cc9-e182-5af0-9a7d-bef61cbf2e4d" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268856 1034 "None" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268856 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533958 true] [17592186268856 1111 #uuid "6fe47129-1269-550d-8ee5-2bdb26d1a369" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268857 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268857 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533958 true] [17592186268857 1111 #uuid "4e465682-6d57-5ceb-a989-175913b5213d" 13194139533958 true] [17592186268858 1017 #edb/ref 17592186